// Expired is the failure of a body that did not finish before its deadline.
type Expired {}

// After runs f as a child task and fails with Expired when d passes first
// (docs/spec/runtime.md, Timeouts). It is an ordinary library function: a
// trailing block is its f argument, and its row parameters give the rows
// that the prototype gave timeout.After by name (README Gap 31). The host
// implements it: it is an extern go binding (grammar.md, Declarations 2).
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/rt.After func After[A, E, R](d duration, f func() A fails E needs R) A fails E | Expired needs R, Scheduler
